From 8d1c651e25e9e0a28f749a71b6d9956bb1effc18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 00:33:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 597/638] base: implement SyncSocket pairs on AROS

AROS has no socketpair() or poll(), so SyncSocket::CreatePair returned
ENOSYS and every audio::OutputStream failed its SyncReader validity
check before reaching the AHI backend.  Build the pair as an in-process
duplex pipe on Lock/ConditionVariable; each endpoint is named by a real
descriptor (open NIL:) so the handle keeps ScopedFD semantics through
mojo::PlatformHandle, with a registry mapping descriptor to endpoint.
Shutdown() has shutdown(SHUT_RDWR) semantics; the destructor closes the
endpoint on AROS so a socket dropped without Close() cannot strand its
peer.
